hey dr. John Bologna here with Ramsey  Network it's good to be back last time  we talked about how we think in pictures  and we speak in words today I want to  tell you about this thing that happened  to me when I was in grad school in this  woman Lisa Pearson who kind of changed  the trajectory of the way I deal with  myself like this idiot that I see in the  mirror right so here's what was going on  I was sitting in a graduate counseling  class so picture this there's a circle  it feels very like kumbaya like we're  all like all how's your feelings right  just how you would picture a graduate  counseling class right and we're all  talking about what would happen if you  were seeing a client for two months  three months six months and one day the  client came in and they were like you're  terrible at this like I've given you  thousands of bucks we did your little  exercise and I asked for the raise I  didn't get it and I took your advice and  she still dumped me right and I said man  that would that would devastate me in  the counseling clinic they all looked at  me like why and I said man that's like  counseling is intimate like you're  you're talking deeply with one another  that would hurt and Lisa Pearson I'll  never forget her she's a good friend and  colleague she said John they don't get  that and I was like oh gosh that was  like stupid counseling he things like  they don't get she said dude they don't  get that and here's what she said she  said you get to decide who hurt your  feelings I was like that sounds  ridiculous what do you mean by that and  she said you get to decide who hurt your  feelings nobody else that day I drove  home on my bike I rode my little bike  home and I walk in the front door and my  son Hank he's like 2 or 3 at the time he  comes out and I said hey buddy and I  went to give him a hug and he looked at  me and he said no daddy and he turned  around and ran the other way down the  hall and my first thought was yeah cuz  you suck as a dad that was my first  thought well then I thought later on  that night about what Lisa had said  about I get to choose who hurt my  feelings and then I thought  Hank is too like he doesn't get a vote  he doesn't get to hurt my feelings  and by the way his favorite game that we  play is chase he just learned how to  walk and I like to chase him around the  house and he loves it and so when I came  in to say hey buddy he wanted to play  and I took it personally so I followed  back up with Lisa and some of my  classmates and I wanted to know more  about this idea of what do you mean I  get to choose who hurt my feelings and  Lisa said she has four did four or five  people who she gave permission to hurt  her feelings and I started going through  my list and I realized I mean I give  permission to people I don't even know  to hurt my feelings I give people  permission who email me mean stuff who  edit my emails and sending back to me  who are always sending negative comments  on the interwebs or students who were  really struggling why was I inviting  them into my heart into my soul and in  my head and giving them permission to  hurt my feelings and then I started  thinking I've got friends that I haven't  talked to in 20 years I've got neighbors  that I don't really know I've got people  at my church and I started one-by-one  pulling people out so this is gonna be  kind of cheesy but no way I started  thinking about it was like this box like  who do I let into this box who'd I get  permission to hurt my feelings and so I  started taking people out I even got to  where I took out my in-laws I love my  in-laws dude I won the lottery with my  in-laws but I decided to not let him  hurt my feelings anymore they can give  me their opinions and give me their  thoughts and their dreams and their  hopes for their daughter and for me  their son-in-law for their grandkids and  then I took my parents out my parents  are incredible they both love me and I  love them but they've got their  experiences and their wisdoms and their  insights but they're not in charge of my  house need my wife are and so I took  them out and suddenly when I stopped  giving people people permission that I  didn't know or I stopped giving people  permission who loved me but who I'm not  gonna let speaking directly into my soul  when I stopped letting them hurt me  I actually was started being able to  hear them in a different way it changed  my relationship it let me love them do  because we could we could relate on a  level that wasn't about me trying to  protect myself from getting hurt but it  was I was able to say coming with tell  me what's going on your heart so my  challenge to you is this find four or  five people who you're gonna give  permission to hurt you when you do  decide on those four or five people  you're gonna get permission to hurt you  let them know and let them know to wield  that power gently let them know that you  love them too this is dr. John Bologna  signing off make sure you subscribe to  get some more genius insights and send  me an email at ask John at Ramsey  solutions calm and I'll answer your  questions directly y'all peace out have  fun and I'll talk to you soon
 

